== Compare the headers' x86 intrinsics with clang's code
# #136: the intrinsics whose instructions no host of the tests runs (XOP's, AVX-NE-CONVERT's, AVX10.2's, SHA512's,
# SM3's, SM4's, MOVRS's, AVX512-BMM's, the extensions' system instructions' and the leaves' of Key Locker, WAITPKG and
# RTM), and controls that run, by clang -O0 and by both paths of this compiler, decoded and followed through
# x86_semantics.c's effects, both paths of a branch: each case's result, stores and effects must be the same
# expressions of its arguments, path by path. Then bf16's arithmetic in a unit whose target has AVX10.2, which clang
# computes in bf16 rather than in float.
./build/compiler test-x86-intrinsics
./build/compiler test-x86-intrinsics --march diamondrapids --option -mno-apxf --cases tests/x86-intrinsics/avx10.2-units.txt
